[quote][b]I'm working on all of these mods on my own.[/b] If you'd like to help, extend or fix one of them, co-author a new one, or join one of my bigger projects, I'm very open to it. Send me a message here on Nexus or on the [b]FarCry:Modding Discord Server[/b].[/quote]

[center][youtube]cB44FdfiZpQ[/youtube][/center]

Changes how the player aims, from the hands to the shot leaving the gun. No damage or AI is changed. Compatibility with weapon behavioral mods.

[b][size=4]What it adds[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Sway[/b] - the breath and a slow wander move the aim, view, gun and shot together; the mouse corrects it as it would a real hand. Each breath rests calmly at the bottom: the moment to time a shot. Down the iron sights the sights also drift out of line as on a real gun.[/*]
[*][b]Heart rate[/b] - from 70 to 170 a minute, climbing as stamina runs down and with wounds or blasts nearby. Each beat jolts the aim; a racing heart breathes faster, sways wider and is heard faintly down a magnifying scope.[/*]
[*][b]Stance[/b] - crouched and still halves the sway; moving widens it.[/*]
[*][b]Hold breath[/b] - on the Dart Rifle, M1903, Dragunov and AS50, hold sprint down the scope to steady the aim for 2 to 4 seconds. Held longer, the hands shake.[/*]
[*][b]Lean[/b] - on Q and E: the upper body leans out about 25 cm past a corner, with the view, arms and gun, and shots leave from where the eye is. Hold to lean, or tap to stay leaned.[/*]
[*][b]Gun near walls[/b] - a gun that would reach into a wall swings down out of it and doesn't fire until it's back up.[/*]
[*][b]Gun blur[/b] - down the iron sights the eye focuses on the front sight, and the rest of the gun goes out of focus, the rear sight most.[/*]
[*][b]Scope eyepiece[/b] - every scope is a black, out-of-focus eyepiece instead of a long tube, with the zoomed view filling its opening, seen through glass. It trails the look a little and kicks back with each shot. The AR-16 and MGL-140 scopes lose their random spread, so a shot goes where the reticle is.[/*]
[*][b]Reticles[/b] - new in every scope: a hunting duplex on the Dart Rifle and M1903, a PSO-1 with its rangefinder on the Dragunov, a red tactical mil-scale on the AS50, and a lit holographic chevron on the AR-16 and MGL-140. They are plain PNG files in bin\plugins\aiming-overhaul\reticles\, so you can swap in your own.[/*]
[*][b]Scope surroundings[/b] - around the eyepiece the world stays at your normal field of view, slightly out of focus, as with both eyes open. No more zooming as the scope comes up.[/*]
[*][b]Scope shadow[/b] - a soft dark crescent from the eyepiece's rim on a fast turn.[/*]
[*][b]Tracers[/b] - from the M249, PKM, Dragunov, AS50 and the mounted machine guns, your own shots included: bright orange streaks, visible however far off. One in six glances off where it lands, up into the air.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Controls[/size][/b]
Two new controls, rebindable in Options → Controls under Movements: [b]Lean left[/b] on Q and [b]Lean right[/b] on E. To free those keys the defaults move: [b]interact to F, throw grenade to G and next throwable to T[/b]. Leaving a vehicle or a mounted gun, a buddy rescue, the machete finish and the watch stay on E and Q, which the game never lets be rebound.

[b][size=4]Settings[/size][/b]
In the [b]Mod Configuration[/b] menu, each effect has its own switch, all on by default: Sway, Hold breath, Gun near walls, Gun blur, Scope shadow, Scope eyepiece, Scope surroundings and Tracers. [b]Iron sight zoom[/b] is there too: switch it off and aiming down iron sights no longer zooms in, while scopes still magnify.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/368]FCSE[/url] 1.4.0 or later, the plugin loader this runs in. Far Cry 2 1.03, Steam or GOG.[/*]
[*]DirectX 9, set in Options → Display → DirectX Version. On DirectX 10 you get the game's own scopes, without the new eyepiece, reticles, surroundings or shadow; the gun blur doesn't show and tracers lose their bright glow.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Installing[/size][/b]
The download is a JackAll layer, which both installers read as-is:
[list]
[*][b]Vortex[/b] - auto-installer handles the rest.[/*]
[*][b]JackAll[/b] - [url=https://jbebe.github.io/farcry-sdk/jackall/installing-mods/]here's a detailed instruction[/url] for JackAll installation.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Compatibility[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Mods that change weapons' stats or data[/b] merge with it field by field.[/*]
[*][b]Mods that change the same fields[/b] (a weapon's tracer settings, its iron-sight effect or its spread down a scope) clash on those fields, and the installer reports it.[/*]
[*][b]Mods that change the controls[/b], such as Flashlight, combine with it control by control. One that rebinds interact, throw grenade or next throwable too clashes on that control, and the installer reports it.[/*]
[/list]
